 "text": "Hi, how are you doing right now? Tent poles help determine where the tent goes. In this case, the spot under the star wheel is the sweet spot, giving you space and views. Set it up there if it suits you. If not, pick the clearest,est spot you can. A hill or bump behind you gives you cold winds. Cut it off completely and redo a long end if it matters. A dead branch can turn into damage that does. Keep a clear circle of about ten feet, so the smoke doesn't get you and the other campers breathe. Good. Pop up the ground sheet and peg two corners well. Then the roof will go on easily.",
